# Dawnhand Dissident's permission is to cast the card, not a cost to cast it for: the card's own alternative cost may be paid (CR
# 601.2b, 118.9), and the three counters are owed "in addition to paying their other costs" (CR 118.8, 601.2f) whatever it is
# cast for. Solitude, exiled with the Dissident, is evoked from exile: Bot1 exiles Swords to Plowshares from its hand for the evoke
# cost and removes three counters from among its creatures (the Dissident's one and its Sylvan Caryatid's two). Solitude enters,
# exiles Bot2's Llanowar Elves (Bot2 gains 1 life) and is sacrificed to evoke (CR 702.74a).

